    <!-- =========================
         ROW_NUMBER WITH PARTITION
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                ROW_NUMBER() with PARTITION BY
            </h2>

            <p>
                <strong>PARTITION BY</strong> divides the result into
                groups. ROW_NUMBER() then starts numbering from
                <strong>1</strong> separately for each group.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>SELECT
    EmployeeId,
    EmployeeName,
    Department,
    Salary,

    ROW_NUMBER() OVER
    (
        PARTITION BY Department
        ORDER BY Salary DESC
    ) AS RowNumber

FROM Employees;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         PRACTICAL EXAMPLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Practical Example
            </h2>

            <p>
                Suppose employees belong to different departments.
                We want to find the highest-paid employee in each
                department.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>WITH EmployeeRanking AS
(
    SELECT
        EmployeeId,
        EmployeeName,
        Department,
        Salary,

        ROW_NUMBER() OVER
        (
            PARTITION BY Department
            ORDER BY Salary DESC
        ) AS RowNumber

    FROM Employees
)

SELECT
    EmployeeId,
    EmployeeName,
    Department,
    Salary

FROM EmployeeRanking

WHERE RowNumber = 1;</code></pre>

            <p class="mt-3 mb-0">
                This query returns the employee with the highest salary
                from each department.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         USE CASES
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Uses of ROW_NUMBER()
            </h2>

            <ul>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Assigning sequential numbers to records.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Finding the first record from each group.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Finding the latest record from each group.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Removing duplicate records.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Implementing pagination.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Finding top records from each category.
                </li>

            </ul>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         IMPORTANT POINTS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="alert alert-warning mb-4">

        <h4 class="fw-bold">
            Important Points
        </h4>

        <ul class="mb-0">

            <li>
                ROW_NUMBER() starts from <strong>1</strong>.
            </li>

            <li>
                ROW_NUMBER() requires the <strong>OVER()</strong> clause.
            </li>

            <li>
                ORDER BY determines the numbering order.
            </li>

            <li>
                PARTITION BY restarts numbering for every group.
            </li>

            <li>
                Each row receives a unique row number within its
                partition.
            </li>

        </ul>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SUMMARY
    ========================== -->

    <div class="p-4 rounded mb-4"
         style="background-color:#cfe2ff;">

        <h2 class="fw-bold">
            Summary
        </h2>

        <p class="mb-0">
            <strong>ROW_NUMBER()</strong> assigns a unique sequential
            number to every row according to the specified ordering.
            When combined with <strong>PARTITION BY</strong>, the
            numbering restarts for each group.
        </p>

    </div>


